@lesson flutter-m02-l09 | MaterialApp | 12
## Learning objectives
- Configure MaterialApp: title, theme, dark theme, home and routes
- Understand what MaterialApp provides to the tree
- Set up debug options

## The root of a Material app
`MaterialApp` wraps your app with everything Material Design widgets need:
- A `Navigator` for routes
- `Theme` (light and dark), `MediaQuery`, `Localizations`
- `ScaffoldMessenger` for SnackBars
- Text direction, title for the OS task switcher, and more

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void main() => runApp(const BimoDemoApp());

class BimoDemoApp extends StatelessWidget {
  const BimoDemoApp({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return MaterialApp(
      title: 'Bimo Demo',
      debugShowCheckedModeBanner: false,
      theme: ThemeData(
        colorScheme: ColorScheme.fromSeed(seedColor: const Color(0xFF6750F5)),
        useMaterial3: true,
      ),
      darkTheme: ThemeData(
        colorScheme: ColorScheme.fromSeed(
          seedColor: const Color(0xFF6750F5),
          brightness: Brightness.dark,
        ),
      ),
      themeMode: ThemeMode.system,
      home: const HomePage(),
    );
  }
}

class HomePage extends StatelessWidget {
  const HomePage({super.key});
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) =>
      const Scaffold(body: Center(child: Text('Welcome to Bimo')));
}
```

## Key properties
- `title`: app name shown by the OS (for example, in the recent apps list on Android).
- `theme`, `darkTheme`, `themeMode`: light/dark themes and which to use (`system`, `light`, `dark`).
- `home`: the first screen.
- `routes`, `initialRoute`, `onGenerateRoute`: named routes (Module 5); for complex apps use `MaterialApp.router` with `go_router`.
- `locale`, `supportedLocales`, `localizationsDelegates`: internationalisation (Module 13).
- `debugShowCheckedModeBanner`: hides the red "DEBUG" banner.

## Material 3
Since Flutter 3.16, `useMaterial3` defaults to `true`. `ColorScheme.fromSeed` generates a complete, accessible palette from one colour. Module 4 dives into theming.

## MaterialApp vs CupertinoApp vs WidgetsApp
- `MaterialApp`: Material Design (Android and cross-platform look).
- `CupertinoApp`: iOS-style widgets and navigation.
- `WidgetsApp`: the minimal base without a design system.

Most apps use `MaterialApp` and adapt specific widgets per platform when needed.

> TIP: Create exactly one `MaterialApp` at the root. Nesting MaterialApps creates separate navigators and themes and causes confusing bugs.

:::check Which property chooses between light and dark themes?
themeMode (system, light or dark).
:::

## Common mistakes
- Creating a new `MaterialApp` inside a screen.
- Defining colours ad hoc throughout the app instead of in the theme.

## Summary
- MaterialApp provides navigation, theming, media queries, localisation and SnackBar support.
- Configure `theme`, `darkTheme` and `themeMode`; set `home` or routes.
- Use one MaterialApp at the root.

## Further learning
- api.flutter.dev ▸ MaterialApp
