> One MaterialApp at the root avoids multiple navigators.

@lesson flutter-m02-l10 | Scaffold | 12
## Learning objectives
- Build screens with Scaffold slots: appBar, body, FAB, navigation, drawer
- Show SnackBars and bottom sheets
- Handle safe areas and keyboard insets

## A screen's skeleton
`Scaffold` implements the basic Material screen layout and positions standard elements correctly:

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

class NotesScreen extends StatelessWidget {
  const NotesScreen({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Scaffold(
      appBar: AppBar(
        title: const Text('My notes'),
        actions: [
          IconButton(icon: const Icon(Icons.search), tooltip: 'Search', onPressed: () {}),
        ],
      ),
      drawer: const Drawer(child: Center(child: Text('Menu'))),
      body: ListView(
        children: const [
          ListTile(title: Text('Shopping list')),
          ListTile(title: Text('Lesson ideas')),
        ],
      ),
      floatingActionButton: FloatingActionButton.extended(
        onPressed: () {
          ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(
            const SnackBar(content: Text('New note created')),
          );
        },
        icon: const Icon(Icons.add),
        label: const Text('New note'),
      ),
      bottomNavigationBar: NavigationBar(
        selectedIndex: 0,
        destinations: const [
          NavigationDestination(icon: Icon(Icons.notes), label: 'Notes'),
          NavigationDestination(icon: Icon(Icons.settings), label: 'Settings'),
        ],
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

## Slots
- `appBar`: top bar with title and actions
- `body`: main content (takes the remaining space)
- `floatingActionButton` (+ `floatingActionButtonLocation`)
- `bottomNavigationBar`: `NavigationBar` or `BottomAppBar`
- `drawer` / `endDrawer`: side menus (opened by the AppBar's menu icon or a swipe)
- `bottomSheet`: a persistent bottom sheet
- `backgroundColor`, `resizeToAvoidBottomInset`

## SnackBars and bottom sheets
```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void showUndo(BuildContext context) {
  ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(
    SnackBar(
      content: const Text('Lesson removed'),
      action: SnackBarAction(label: 'Undo', onPressed: () {}),
    ),
  );
}

Future<void> showOptions(BuildContext context) {
  return showModalBottomSheet<void>(
    context: context,
    showDragHandle: true,
    builder: (context) => const SafeArea(
      child: Column(mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min, children: [
        ListTile(leading: Icon(Icons.share), title: Text('Share')),
        ListTile(leading: Icon(Icons.delete), title: Text('Delete')),
      ]),
    ),
  );
}
```

## Safe areas and the keyboard
`Scaffold` automatically avoids system bars for its app bar and handles the keyboard: with `resizeToAvoidBottomInset: true` (the default), the body shrinks when the keyboard opens so text fields stay visible. For content without an app bar (like a full-screen image), wrap it in `SafeArea` to avoid notches and status bars.

> TIP: Each route (screen) usually has its own Scaffold. Don't nest Scaffolds inside each other unless you know why.

:::check Which object shows SnackBars in modern Flutter?
ScaffoldMessenger, via ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(...).
:::

## Common mistakes
- Nesting Scaffolds, producing double app bars or wrong keyboard handling.
- Putting content under the status bar on screens without an AppBar; use SafeArea.

## Summary
- Scaffold provides slots for app bar, body, FAB, navigation bar, drawers and sheets.
- Use ScaffoldMessenger for SnackBars and showModalBottomSheet for sheets.
- Scaffold handles insets; use SafeArea where there's no app bar.

## Further learning
- api.flutter.dev ▸ Scaffold
